            <ArticleTitle>Dissection of ascending aorta. A new cause of alveolar hemorrhage?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>327-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Alveolar hemorrhage is an entity caused by different etiologies. We report the case of a male who was admitted in our Service due to hemoptysis secondary to an alveolar hemorrhage diagnosed by chest X-ray and fiberoptic bronchoscopy. Thirty six hours after the admission the patient died and his necropsy showed dissection of ascending aorta and alveolar hemorrhage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
